---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Meyppi terms of service for campaign delivery audits."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: 1 October 2026</p>

      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        Meyppi provides independent campaign delivery audits: verification
        of whether contracted creatives appeared in published media, which
        version appeared, when, and whether delivery was complete. Audits
        are a fixed-fee paid service.
      </p>

      <h2>Evidence, not legal proof</h2>
      <p>
        Meyppi reports algorithmic findings from acoustic fingerprint
        evidence. Results are classified as Detected, Not Detected,
        Insufficient Signal, or Manual Review Required, each with
        confidence and methodology. Meyppi does not warrant results as
        legal proof, and confidence values must not be presented as such.
      </p>

      <h2>Media and permission</h2>
      <p>
        Clients are responsible for having the right to provide the
        creatives and media they submit. Meyppi processes material only
        from permitted sources and records the permission basis and
        evidence tier for every item.
      </p>

      <h2>Fees</h2>
      <p>
        Campaign audits are charged as a fixed fee (₹15,000–₹25,000 for a
        standard campaign, scaling with creatives, publishers, episodes,
        and lookback). Fees are agreed in writing before work begins. No
        annual contracts. No hidden usage charges in V1.
      </p>

      <h2>Scope</h2>
      <p>
        V1 covers pre-produced audio creatives in podcast and digital
        audio content where the published media is independently
        observable. Dynamic ad insertion, host-read verification, and
        video sources are outside V1 scope.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of India.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .narrow {
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .muted {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
</style>
